%N A401753 Escape time of Langton's ant on an n X k rectangular grid: T(n,k) for 1 <= k <= n, read by rows.
%C A401753 The escape time T(n,k) denotes the maximum number of steps that Langton's ant can perform within a rectangular grid with n columns and k rows before escaping the grid, taken over all possible starting positions and orientations of the ant and all possible initial color configurations of the grid. Note that T(n,k) = T(k,n).
%C A401753 The configurations achieving the corresponding escape times can be found at the Etse link below.
%H A401753 Kossi Roland Etse, <a href="https://ekroland.github.io/TEA/">Escape Time Configurations</a>.
%H A401753 Kossi Roland Etse, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2026.49">How Long Can The Escaping Ant Be Confined?</a>, in 51st International Symposium on Mathematical Foundations of Computer Science (MFCS 2026), Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), Volume 386, Article 49, pp. 49:1-49:17, Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik, 2026. See Table 1.
%H A401753 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a401/A401753.java">Java program</a> (github)
%H A401753 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Langton&#39;s_ant">Langton's ant</a>.
%F A401753 T(n,n) = A282425(n) + 1.
